---
import '../styles/studio.css';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="Your local studio for images, illustrations and experiments."/><title>Atelier — Local Image Studio</title></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="/studio/" aria-label="Atelier home"><span class="brand-mark">a.</span> atelier<span class="local">LOCAL</span></a><nav><a href="#workspace">Create</a><a href="#explore">Explore</a><a href="#library">Image library</a><a href="#guide">Guide</a></nav><span id="health" role="status">Connecting …</span></header>
<main><section class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SPACE FOR YOUR VISUAL IDEAS</p><h1>From idea to image<span>.</span></h1><p>Anima Aesthetic with trained Low Poly styles, MOSS, Qwen Image 2.1 and Krea Pixel Art. Choose a recipe and describe your subject.</p></div><div class="private-note"><span class="dot"></span> On your computer.<br/>Your images stay here.</div></section>
<div id="message" role="alert" hidden></div>
<section id="workspace" class="workspace"><form id="generate" class="controls"><div class="section-title"><h2>Your creation</h2><span>01 — CREATE</span></div>
<label for="model">Model</label><div class="row"><select id="model" name="model" required></select><button type="button" id="load" class="quiet">Load</button></div><p id="model-note" class="hint"></p><a id="license" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="small-link">Model & license ↗</a>
<select id="mode" hidden><option value="text">Text → Image</option></select>
<label for="workflow">Workflow</label><select id="workflow"><option value="guided">Guided · fill in a recipe</option><option value="free">Free prompt · custom settings</option></select>
<div id="guided-fields"><label for="recipe">Image recipe</label><select id="recipe"></select><p id="recipe-description" class="hint"></p>
<p id="recipe-tip" class="hint" hidden></p>
<fieldset id="modeling-fields" hidden><legend>Blender reference</legend><label for="modeling-view">Image purpose and view</label><select id="modeling-view" aria-describedby="modeling-note"></select><div id="modeling-asset-fields"><label for="modeling-asset">Asset type</label><select id="modeling-asset"></select><button id="modeling-example" type="button" class="quiet">Use Blender starter</button></div><p id="modeling-note" class="hint">One clear modeling concept with neutral light and simple materials. Separate AI views can change the design; matching blueprints need a shared 3D blockout. <a class="small-link" href="/studio/lowpoly-guide/#blender">Blender workflow ↗</a></p></fieldset>
<label for="subject">What would you like to create?</label><textarea id="subject" rows="3" maxlength="2000" placeholder="For example: an adult mage with red hair and a green cloak"></textarea>
<label for="scene"><span id="scene-label">Setting or action</span> <span class="optional">optional</span></label><textarea id="scene" rows="2" maxlength="2000" placeholder="Leave blank to use the recipe’s default setting"></textarea>
<label for="scene-details"><span id="details-label">Extra details</span> <span class="optional">optional</span></label><textarea id="scene-details" rows="2" maxlength="2000" placeholder="For example: glowing crystals, wind moving the cloak"></textarea>
<div id="visible-text-fields" hidden><label for="visible-text">Visible text <span class="optional">optional · exact wording</span></label><textarea id="visible-text" rows="2" maxlength="600" placeholder="For example: EXPLORE"></textarea><p class="hint">Qwen renders this wording in the image. Keep it short and check the spelling in the result.</p></div><button id="example" type="button" class="quiet">Use example</button>
<label for="aspect-ratio">Aspect ratio</label><select id="aspect-ratio"><option value="auto">Recommended · recipe format</option></select><p id="format-note" class="hint" role="status"></p><label for="recipe-quality">Quality</label><select id="recipe-quality"><option value="preview">Draft · faster</option><option value="standard" selected>Recommended</option><option value="detail">More detail · slower</option></select>
<p class="hint">You choose the subject. The recipe selects the model and adds composition, lighting, style, size and settings. English is the recommended starting point for these models; other languages are passed through as entered.</p>
<details><summary>View full prompt and settings</summary><pre id="recipe-preview">Enter a subject to preview the full prompt and settings.</pre></details></div>
<div id="free-fields" hidden>
<label for="prompt">What would you like to see?</label><textarea id="prompt" rows="5" required maxlength="14000" placeholder="A small café on a rain-soaked street. Warm light shines through the windows, and a red bicycle stands by the door."></textarea>
<label for="preset">Style preset</label><select id="preset"></select><p id="preset-tip" class="hint"></p>
<div id="style-fields"><label for="suffix">Style suffix <span class="optional">editable</span></label><textarea id="suffix" rows="2"></textarea></div>
<label for="quality">Quality profile</label><select id="quality"></select><label for="size">Image size</label><select id="size"><option value="1024x1024">1:1 · Square · 1024 × 1024</option><option value="1024x576">16:9 · Landscape · 1024 × 576</option><option value="576x1024">9:16 · Portrait · 576 × 1024</option><option value="1024x768">4:3 · Landscape · 1024 × 768</option><option value="768x1024">3:4 · Portrait · 768 × 1024</option><option value="1152x768">3:2 · Landscape · 1152 × 768</option><option value="768x1152">2:3 · Portrait · 768 × 1152</option><option value="768x768">Draft · 768 × 768</option><option value="512x512">Quick test · 512 × 512</option></select>
</div><div id="pixel-fields" hidden><div class="pair"><div><label for="pixel-grid">Pixel grid</label><select id="pixel-grid"><option value="32">32 · chunky icons</option><option value="64" selected>64 · characters and tiles</option><option value="128">128 · detailed scenes</option></select></div><div><label for="pixel-colors">Palette</label><select id="pixel-colors"><option value="16">16 colors</option><option value="24" selected>24 colors</option><option value="32">32 colors</option><option value="64">64 colors</option><option value="128">128 colors</option></select></div></div><p class="hint">Generate at 1024 × 1024, then clean the grid and palette. Download the large preview or the native pixel PNG. Other aspect ratios keep square pixels and adjust the native dimensions.</p><a class="small-link" href="/studio/pixel-guide/">Pixel art tips and examples ↗</a></div><details id="expert-settings"><summary>Advanced settings</summary><div class="pair"><div><label for="steps">Steps</label><input id="steps" type="number" min="1" max="100" required/></div><div><label for="cfg">CFG</label><input id="cfg" type="number" min="1" max="12" step="0.1" required/></div></div><label for="sampler">Sampler</label><select id="sampler"></select><label for="negative">Negative prompt</label><textarea id="negative" rows="2" maxlength="16000" placeholder="Optional: features to avoid"></textarea><p class="hint">Only the prompt shown here is used. No content filtering or automatic rewriting.</p><div class="pair"><div><label for="seed">Seed</label><input id="seed" type="number" min="0" max="2147483647" placeholder="Random"/></div><div><label for="count">Batch size</label><input id="count" type="number" value="1" min="1" max="8"/></div></div><p class="hint">A fixed seed helps compare results within the same model. Each image in a batch increments the seed.</p></details>
<div id="edit-options" hidden><label for="upload">Reference image</label><input id="upload" type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp"/><p class="hint">PNG, JPEG or WebP · up to 12 MiB. The image is fitted to the selected output size.</p><label for="strength">Strength <output id="strength-value">0.65</output></label><input id="strength" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.65"/><div id="mask-options" hidden><div class="pair"><div><label for="brush">Brush size</label><input id="brush" type="range" min="5" max="120" value="35"/></div><div><label for="feather">Feathering (px)</label><input id="feather" type="number" min="0" max="32" value="8"/></div></div><div class="row"><button type="button" id="eraser" aria-pressed="false" class="quiet">Eraser</button><button type="button" id="undo" class="quiet">Undo</button><button type="button" id="clear-mask" class="quiet">Clear</button></div><label for="mask-upload">Or upload a black-and-white mask</label><input id="mask-upload" type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp"/><label for="zoom">Zoom</label><input id="zoom" type="range" min="1" max="3" step="0.25" value="1"/><p class="hint">Areas marked in orange are regenerated. The original is preserved outside the mask.</p></div></div>
<button class="primary" id="submit" type="submit">Generate image <span>↗</span></button><p class="save-note">Results and settings are saved locally.</p></form>
<div class="visual"><div class="section-title"><h2>Preview</h2><span id="preview-label">YOUR NEXT IDEA</span></div><div id="preview" class="preview"><div id="empty" class="empty"><div class="abstract"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><h3>Something new starts here.</h3><p>Describe your idea and choose a style.<br/>Your image will appear right here.</p></div><img id="result" hidden alt="Current result"/><div id="editor" hidden><img id="reference" alt="Reference image"/><canvas id="mask" aria-label="Press and drag to draw a mask"></canvas></div></div><div class="preview-actions"><a id="download" class="quiet button" hidden download="atelier.png">Download PNG ↓</a><a id="download-pixels" class="quiet button" hidden download="atelier-pixels.png">Download native pixels ↓</a><button id="reuse-reference" type="button" class="quiet" hidden>Use as reference</button></div><section class="queue"><div class="section-title"><h2>Jobs</h2><span id="queue-count">0 ACTIVE</span></div><div id="jobs"><p class="hint">No jobs yet. Every good idea starts somewhere.</p></div></section></div></section>
<section id="explore" class="recipe-browser" aria-labelledby="explore-title"><div class="section-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">PICK A LOOK</p><h2 id="explore-title">Recipes worth exploring</h2></div><span id="recipe-total" role="status"></span></div><p class="hint">Real examples generated with these models. “Use this example” restores the recorded inputs, quality and seed so you can start from the picture you like.</p><div class="recipe-filters"><div><label for="recipe-model-filter">Browse by model</label><select id="recipe-model-filter"><option value="all">All models</option></select></div><div><label for="recipe-search">Find a look</label><input id="recipe-search" type="search" placeholder="Try retro, clay, portrait or sticker"/></div></div><div id="recipe-gallery" class="recipe-grid"></div><button id="more-recipes" class="quiet" type="button" hidden>Show more recipes</button></section><section id="library" class="library"><div class="section-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR COLLECTION</p><h2>Image library</h2></div><div class="row"><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="only-favorites"/> Favorites</label><button id="compare" type="button" class="quiet">Compare 2 images</button></div></div><p class="hint">Select images to delete, or select exactly two to compare side by side.</p><div class="selection-tools"><button id="select-all" class="quiet" type="button">Select all displayed</button><button id="clear-selection" class="quiet" type="button" disabled>Clear selection</button><span id="selection-count" role="status">0 selected</span><button id="delete-selected" class="quiet danger" type="button" disabled>Delete selected</button></div><div id="gallery" class="gallery"></div><button id="more-images" type="button" class="quiet" hidden>Load more images</button></section>
<section id="guide" class="guide"><div><p class="eyebrow">GET STARTED</p><h2>Your subject.<br/>The rest is ready.</h2></div><div><h3>Anime with Anima Aesthetic</h3><p>Choose a character portrait, fantasy, film scene, neon night, landscape, slice of life, manga, watercolor or chibi. Only the subject is required. Setting and details are optional.</p><p>“Use example” gives you a complete starting point. Start by changing only the character or subject. Recipes use no score_* tags or automatic content tags.</p><h3>Low Poly with MOSS</h3><p>Use Anything for arbitrary low-poly motifs, Track overview for a complete circuit, or the dedicated character, kart, prop, building and scene recipes. Blender reference prepares simple forms, clear silhouettes and neutral light with no additional style adapter.</p><a href="/studio/lowpoly-guide/">MOSS Low Poly guide and examples ↗</a><h3>Realistic photography with MOSS</h3><p>Choose natural portrait, candid everyday, street documentary, cinematic still, product studio, landscape, interior or food. Use “Recommended” for realistic detail: 50 steps, CFG 3 and a suitable image size. “Draft” is for trying the composition.</p><h3>Low Poly with MOSS</h3><p>Choose a floating diorama, a 1990s game scene or an angular game world. The recipe adds visible polygon faces, flat shading, and suitable camera and lighting.</p></div><div><h3>Qwen Image 2.1</h3><p>Try graphic posters, illustrated covers, editorial portraits, product scenes, isometric worlds and transparent stickers. The optional “Visible text” field supplies exact wording. Qwen uses a non-commercial research license; see the model link.</p><h3>Krea Pixel Art</h3><p>Choose a loot icon, adventure character, isometric hideaway or scenic world. The recipe selects a 32, 64 or 128 pixel LoRA and a small palette. Eight steps are recommended. Download a crisp large preview and a native pixel PNG.</p><a href="/studio/pixel-guide/">Pixel art guide and examples ↗</a><h3>When the image misses the mark</h3><p>Describe specific shapes, clothing, actions and positions. Start with one main character. Keep the seed fixed and change one field at a time. “More detail” cannot replace a clear composition.</p><h3>Guided or free prompt</h3><p>Guided mode prepares the full prompt and settings. You can inspect everything under “View full prompt and settings”. “Free prompt” gives you direct control over the settings.</p><a href="/studio/anima-guide/">Detailed guide and examples ↗</a></div></section>
</main><footer><span>atelier / local image studio</span><span>Your ideas. Your models. Your computer.</span></footer>
<dialog id="auth"><form id="auth-form"><h2>Connect to the service</h2><p>This service requires an API key. It is kept only in this tab’s memory.</p><label for="key">API key</label><input id="key" type="password" autocomplete="off" required/><button class="primary" type="submit">Connect</button></form></dialog>
<dialog id="detail"><button class="close quiet" type="button" data-close="detail" aria-label="Close">×</button><img id="detail-image" alt="Saved image"/><pre id="metadata"></pre><div class="row"><button id="reuse" class="primary" type="button">Reuse settings</button><button id="favorite" class="quiet" type="button">Favorite</button><button id="delete-image" class="quiet danger" type="button">Delete image</button></div></dialog>
<dialog id="delete-confirm" aria-labelledby="delete-title"><h2 id="delete-title">Delete image?</h2><p id="delete-description">The PNG and its saved settings will be permanently deleted.</p><div class="row"><button id="delete-cancel" class="quiet" type="button">Cancel</button><button id="delete-confirm-button" class="quiet danger" type="button">Delete permanently</button></div></dialog>
<dialog id="recipe-example" aria-labelledby="example-title"><button class="close quiet" type="button" data-close="recipe-example" aria-label="Close">×</button><h2 id="example-title"></h2><img id="example-image" alt=""/><p id="example-settings" class="hint"></p><pre id="example-metadata"></pre><a id="example-native" class="quiet button" hidden download>Download native pixels ↓</a><button id="use-preview-example" class="primary" type="button">Use this example</button></dialog><dialog id="comparison"><button class="close quiet" type="button" data-close="comparison" aria-label="Close">×</button><h2>One view. Two possibilities.</h2><div id="comparison-images" class="comparison"></div></dialog>
<script>import '../scripts/studio.js';</script></body></html>
